We are building a receipt calculator: 

You have been hired by QuickCart Retail to build the core processing engine for their
 new digital point-of-sale system. The front-end layout is complete, but the interface
  requires a JavaScript module to validate customer order inputs, generate line-item
   summaries, and construct an encoded security barcode string for every transaction.


Everyone starts with the same HTML Starter Code.  You build style.css (using AI,
 then we shut it off)


<!doctype html>
<html>
    <head>
        <title>QuickCart Order Processor</title>
        <meta charset="utf-8">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/style.css">
        
    </head>
    <body>
        <main>
            <header>
                <h1>QuickCart Receipt System</h1>
            </header>
           
            <label for="itemCount">Quantity:</label>
            <input type="number" id="itemCount">
           
            <label for="itemDescription">Product Name / Note:</label>
            <textarea id="itemDescription" rows="5"></textarea>
           
            <input type="button" value="Process Order" onClick="processOrder()">
           
            <div id="receiptOutput"></div>
        </main>
    </body>
</html>

